# Component Patterns

## Atomic Design Structure

Components follow Atomic Design methodology:

### Atoms (`src/components/atoms/`)
Smallest, indivisible components:
- Buttons, inputs, labels, icons
- Single responsibility
- Highly reusable
- Examples: `loading-button.tsx`, `password-input.tsx`, `theme-switcher.tsx`

### Molecules (`src/components/molecules/`)
Combinations of atoms:
- Form fields with labels
- Search bars, date pickers
- Examples: `autocomplete-input.tsx`, `search-bar.tsx`, `date-range-picker.tsx`

### Organisms (`src/components/organisms/`)
Complex, self-contained sections:
- Data tables, sidebars, navigation
- May contain state and logic
- Examples: `data-table/`, `sidebar.tsx`, `navbar.tsx`

### Templates (`src/components/templates/`)
Page-level layouts:
- Define page structure
- Use server/client split pattern
- Examples: `dashboard/dashboard.server.tsx`

### UI (`src/components/ui/`)
shadcn/ui components - **DO NOT MODIFY** unless customizing variants.
Add new shadcn components using: `npx shadcn@latest add <component>`

## File Naming Conventions

| Pattern | Purpose | Example |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `*.server.tsx` | Server components | `inventory.server.tsx` |
| `*.client.tsx` | Client components | `inventory.client.tsx` |
| `*.stories.tsx` | Storybook stories | `button.stories.tsx` |
| `index.ts` | Barrel exports | `index.ts` |

## Server/Client Split Pattern

Templates and complex components use this pattern for data prefetching:

```typescript
// warehouses.server.tsx - Server Component
import { HydrationBoundaryProvider } from '@/providers/hydration-boundary-provider';
import { prefetchWarehouses } from '../api/lib/warehouse.prefetch';
import { WarehousesClientTemplate } from './warehouses.client';

export const WarehousesTemplate = async () => {
  const queryClient = await prefetchWarehouses();
  
  return (
    <HydrationBoundaryProvider queryClient={queryClient}>
      <WarehousesClientTemplate />
    </HydrationBoundaryProvider>
  );
};
```

```typescript
// warehouses.client.tsx - Client Component
'use client';

import { useWarehouses } from '../hooks/query/use-warehouses';

export const WarehousesClientTemplate = () => {
  const { data: warehouses } = useWarehouses();
  
  return (
    // Component JSX
  );
};
```

## Styling Patterns

### Always use cn() for class merging

```typescript
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

interface ButtonProps {
  className?: string;
}

export const Button = ({ className }: ButtonProps) => {
  return (
    <button className={cn('px-4 py-2 rounded-md', className)}>
      Click me
    </button>
  );
};
```

### CVA for Component Variants

Use `class-variance-authority` for components with variants:

```typescript
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

const buttonVariants = cva(
  'inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-colors',
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90',
        destructive: 'bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90',
        outline: 'border border-input bg-background hover:bg-accent',
      },
      size: {
        default: 'h-10 px-4 py-2',
        sm: 'h-9 rounded-md px-3',
        lg: 'h-11 rounded-md px-8',
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: 'default',
      size: 'default',
    },
  }
);

interface ButtonProps extends VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {
  className?: string;
}

export const Button = ({ variant, size, className }: ButtonProps) => {
  return (
    <button className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size }), className)}>
      Click me
    </button>
  );
};
```

### Use Semantic Color Tokens

Always use CSS variable-based colors from the theme:

```typescript
// Good - uses semantic tokens
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border" />
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground" />
<div className="bg-muted text-muted-foreground" />
<div className="bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground" />

// Avoid - hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-white text-black" />
```

### Dark Mode Support

Dark mode is handled automatically via CSS variables and `next-themes`.
Use the `dark:` prefix only when the semantic tokens don't suffice.

## Stories Organization

Stories are co-located in `stories/` subdirectories:

```
components/
├── atoms/
│   ├── loading-button.tsx
│   └── stories/
│       └── loading-button.stories.tsx
```

Story file structure:

```typescript
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/nextjs-vite';
import { LoadingButton } from '../loading-button';

const meta = {
  title: 'Atoms/LoadingButton',
  component: LoadingButton,
} satisfies Meta<typeof LoadingButton>;

export default meta;
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>;

export const Default: Story = {
  args: {
    children: 'Submit',
  },
};

export const Loading: Story = {
  args: {
    children: 'Submit',
    isLoading: true,
  },
};
```

## Component Export Pattern

Use barrel exports for clean imports:

```typescript
// components/atoms/index.ts
export { LoadingButton } from './loading-button';
export { PasswordInput } from './password-input';
export { ThemeSwitcher } from './theme-switcher';
```

## Accessibility

- Always include proper ARIA attributes
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Include focus-visible styles: `focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px]`
